![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The current implementation of `runFullBetaTextOnlyRuntimeSmoke` does not handle cases where the posture map file is missing or malformed, which will result in unhandled exceptions. Additionally, if the posture map is empty or malformed such that no attemptable text-only rows are loaded, the registry will have 0 questions and the smoke test will silently pass with 0 samples. To ensure robust fail-closed behavior, wrap the registry loading and sample execution in a try-catch block and explicitly verify that the number of loaded samples is greater than 0.

